**Mathematical Model:**

Let $I$ be the set of all products listed above.

**Decision Variables:**
- $x_i$: Number of units of product $i$ to fulfill for customer purchases, for each product $i \in I$.

**Objective:**
\[
\max \sum_{i \in I} r_i x_i
\]

**Constraints:**
- Inventory and demand fulfillment:
  \[
  0 \leq x_i \leq \min\{d_i, s_i\} \qquad \forall i \in I
  \]
  (You cannot fulfill more than available inventory or demand for any product.)

- Integrality:
  \[
  x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \qquad \forall i \in I
  \]

**Where:**
- $r_i$ = Revenue per unit for product $i$ (from 'Revenue' column)
- $d_i$ = Demand for product $i$ (from 'Demand' column)
- $s_i$ = Initial Inventory for product $i$ (from 'Initial Inventory' column)

**Complete Formulation:**

\[
\begin{align*}
\max \quad & \sum_{i \in I} r_i x_i \\
\text{s.t.} \quad & 0 \leq x_i \leq \min\{d_i, s_i\} \qquad \forall i \in I \\
& x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \qquad \forall i \in I
\end{align*}
\]

